27um|n|Woad. ; A little mass, tuft, or bundle, as of hay or tow. ; Specifically: A little mass of some soft or flexible material, such as hay, straw, tow, paper, or old rope yarn, used for retaining a charge of powder in a gun, or for keeping the powder and shot close; also, to diminish or avoid the effects of windage. Also, by extension, a dusk of felt, pasteboard, etc., serving a similar purpose. ; A soft mass, especially of some loose, fibrous substance, used for various purposes, as for stopping an aperture, padding a garment, etc. ; Alt. of Wadd	n:lwl,141,4~lwl,141,4	N:rqc,31,4~rqc,31,4
