27v5|n|A thin cake made of flour and other ingredients. ; A thin cake or piece of bread (commonly unleavened, circular, and stamped with a crucifix or with the sacred monogram) used in the Eucharist, as in the Roman Catholic Church. ; An adhesive disk of dried paste, made of flour, gelatin, isinglass, or the like, and coloring matter, -- used in sealing letters and other documents.	a:328,166,3~328,166,3	n:328,151,1;16fj,120,6;1upg,93,2~16fj,120,6;1upg,93,2;328,151,1	N:6ks,69,7~6ks,69,7
