27vi|n|To pledge; to hazard on the event of a contest; to stake; to bet, to lay; to wager; as, to wage a dollar. ; To expose one's self to, as a risk; to incur, as a danger; to venture; to hazard. ; To engage in, as a contest, as if by previous gage or pledge; to carry on, as a war. ; To adventure, or lay out, for hire or reward; to hire out. ; To put upon wages; to hire; to employ; to pay wages to. ; To give security for the performance of. ; To bind one's self; to engage. ; That which is staked or ventured; that for which one incurs risk or danger; prize; gage. ; That for which one labors; meed; reward; stipulated payment for service performed; hire; pay; compensation; -- at present generally used in the plural. See Wages.	a:18lq,89,7;ds8,84,6;3a3,80,6;ykn,76,3;1asb,75,5;5p3,36,3;16y3,25,3;16xy,24,5;7ey,7,3~18lq,89,7;ds8,84,6;3a3,80,6;16xy,24,5;1asb,75,5;7ey,7,3;5p3,36,3;16y3,25,3;ykn,76,3	n:16jb,63,6;5p3,20,1~16jb,63,6;5p3,20,1	N:2810,70,6;15h0,39,2;1sai,35,2;13tv,32,5;k03,24,4;1o59,22,3;221c,1,2~2810,70,6;13tv,32,5;k03,24,4;1o59,22,3;221c,1,2;1sai,35,2;15h0,39,2
