285t|a|An addition to the shares representing the capital of a stock company so that the aggregate par value of the shares is increased while their value for investment is diminished, or "diluted." ; To wet or supply with water; to moisten; to overflow with water; to irrigate; as, to water land; to water flowers. ; To supply with water for drink; to cause or allow to drink; as, to water cattle and horses. ; To wet and calender, as cloth, so as to impart to it a lustrous appearance in wavy lines; to diversify with wavelike lines; as, to water silk. Cf. Water, n., 6. ; To shed, secrete, or fill with, water or liquid matter; as, his eyes began to water. ; To get or take in water; as, the ship put into port to water.	j:yuq,77,1;doa,41,1;1vmw,6,1~1vmw,6,1;doa,41,1;yuq,77,1
