287p|v|To increase in size; to grow bigger; to become larger or fuller; -- opposed to wane. ; To pass from one state to another; to become; to grow; as, to wax strong; to wax warmer or colder; to wax feeble; to wax old; to wax worse and worse. ; To smear or rub with wax; to treat with wax; as, to wax a thread or a table.	s:1gb3,74,1;may,69,1;mrn,44,1;zc7,27,1~may,69,1;zc7,27,1;mrn,44,1;1gb3,74,1
